r hound guards the gate of the night","the patient sister who waits outside the sun's door"],"poetic":["the moon that sees the lovers home","which keeps watch over sleeping towns","thin as a fingernail and twice as sharp","the colour of milk spilled on a dark table","pale and patient, like an old friend","which seems to follow you down every road","the last light on the water before the tide turns","which night-shift workers wave to on the way home","hanging low over the harbour like a lamp left on","which wears the clouds like a shawl","the moon you only notice when you cannot sleep","silver and silent over the snow","which pulls at the sea and at the heart","never quite full, never quite gone","which lights the way for the lost and the late","which the wolves sing to, and the poets steal from","thin and bright in the first cold of autumn","which turns the rooftops to pewter","the one the children say is made of glass","like a coin at the bottom of a deep well","which shows its whole face only to the patient","which rises late and leaves early","like a lantern carried home across the fields","which makes even the dullest pond look magical","shining on the empty swings in the park"]}}}